<Marketing
  title="Grossline — privacy"
  description="What Grossline reads, what it deliberately never collects, how it's protected, and how to have it deleted."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <div class="pagehead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Privacy</div>
      <h1>What we hold, and what we don't.</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 15 September 2026</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="prose-section" style="padding-top:48px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Grossline produces a monthly reporting service for Shopify brands. To do that we read
          data from the platforms you already use. This page explains exactly what we read, what we
          leave alone, and what happens to it. It's written to match what the software actually
          does.
        </p>

        <h2>What we read</h2>
        <p>With the read-only access you grant us, we read:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <b>Your Shopify store</b> — orders and their amounts, products, and the sales history we
            need to work out what you kept.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>Your Google Ads and Meta ad accounts</b> — how much you spent, by account and
            campaign. We can't spend your money or change a campaign.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>Your contact details</b> — the name and email you give us so we can send your report
            and talk to you.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What we deliberately never collect</h2>
        <p>
          We do not collect your customers' names, email addresses, phone numbers or delivery
          addresses. The software is built to leave that data behind: from Shopify we take only an
          anonymous customer reference, an order count and a lifetime-spend figure — never the
          identifying fields. We never receive card or bank details. And we never write anything
          back to your store or your ad accounts.
        </p>

        <h2>How we use it</h2>
        <p>
          Your data is used for one thing: producing your reports. We do not sell data, we do not
          share one brand's data with another, we do not use it for advertising, and we do not build
          profiles across brands.
        </p>
        <p>
          To help draft the wording of a report, the report's computed figures may be sent to an AI
          provider that turns them into plain-English sentences. Only the calculated numbers are
          sent — and since we hold no customer personal data, none is involved. When that step is
          switched off, the report uses fixed templates instead. Our providers are listed on our
          <a href="/data-processing">data processing</a> page.
        </p>

        <h2>How it's protected</h2>
        <p>
          The access credentials you grant are encrypted where they're stored. Each brand's data is
          isolated at the database level so one engagement can never read another's. Access is
          limited to the analyst preparing your reports.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it, and deleting it</h2>
        <p>
          When you start, we pull roughly the last thirteen months so your first report has
          history to compare against. We keep your data while your engagement is active. When you
          leave, your platform credentials are revoked and your data is deleted on request to
          <a href="mailto:hello@getgrossline.com">hello@getgrossline.com</a> — this removes your
          orders, cost data, computed figures, reports and connection records.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it, at
          any time. You can also revoke our access from inside Shopify, Google or Meta yourself,
          which stops any further reading immediately.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy, or a request about your data:
          <a href="mailto:hello@getgrossline.com">hello@getgrossline.com</a>. Grossline is based in
          Ahmedabad, India.
        </p>
      </div>
